          <Message>Nightly ChaosRandom/Stress tier: slow for the PR suite, and surfaces an unresolved leader-side commit hole under continuous multi-partition faults. Out-of-order per-proposal commit (RaftWriteAhead.EnqueueCommit advances commitIndex non-contiguously) strands an entry as Proposed below the leader's in-memory frontier; GetRangeAsync (Committed-only) can never re-ship it, so followers buffer later entries over the permanent hole and convergence times out. Needs a commit-model fix (gap-aware leader commit + stalled-proposal re-drive). The non-contiguous-delivery bug and the CommitMonotonicity dip artifact it was previously blocked on are both fixed.</Message>
        </ErrorInfo>
      </Output>
    </UnitTestResult>
    <UnitTestResult executionId="110161b7-9755-4115-979d-f2fb4cc93a6f" testId="f94d740b-fdd2-ca92-96fa-9d655f3caf39" testName="Kommander.Tests.LoadReports.TestBuildLocalLoadReport.BuildLocalLoadReport_NewlyLedPartition_IsExcludedByStabilityGate" computerName="Bacons-Mac-mini" duration="00:00:00.0047043" startTime="2026-08-23T16:50:47.7845320-05:00" endTime="2026-08-23T16:50:47.7892440-05:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="110161b7-9755-4115-979d-f2fb4cc93a6f" />
